cxd4 9. a3 Be7 10. exd4 Qc7 11. b4 Ng4 12. g3 f5 13. Nc3 d6 14. h3 Nf6 15. Qe2
Bxf3 16. Qxf3 Nc6 17. Qe3 Qd7 18. d5 exd5 19. cxd5 Ne5 20. Bb5 Qb7 21. Rd1 a6
22. Bf1 Rfe8 23. Bb2 Bf8 24. Ne2 Kh8 25. Qb3 a5 26. Nd4 a4 27. Qc2 f4 28. gxf4
Ng6 29. Ne6 Nh4 30. Bxf6 gxf6 31. Qe2 Bh6 32. Qh5 Rxe6 33. Qxh6 Rg8+ 34. Kh1 f5
35. Qxe6 $4 (35. Qxh4 $18 Qg7 $140 36. Qg3 Rg6 37. Qf3) 35... Qg7 36. Qxg8+
Kxg8 37. Rdc1 Qb2 38. Rc8+ Kg7 39. Rc7+ Kh6 40. Re1 Qxf2 41. Re6+ Ng6 42. Bg2
Qxf4 43. Rc6 Qf2 44. Rexd6 f4 45. Rf6 Kg5 46. Rf7 Nh4 47. Rg7+ Kf5 48. Rf7+ Kg5
{Sources: BCM, February 1957, p31; CHESS, Vol.22, No.284-5, January 1957, p105}
(48... Kg5 {... a draw was agreed on the proposal of Black. But Horseman
failed to observe that he now had a won game, since after} 49. Rg7+ Ng6 50. Rf7
({Stockfish 15:} 50. Rxh7 $1 {seems to indicate that Szabo could have rescued
a draw with best play anyway:}) 50... Ne5 {White cannot prevent an eventual f3
with an easy win for Black" (Golombek, BCM)}) 1/2-1/2

