1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. e3 c5 5. Bd3 d5 6. Nf3 O-O 7. O-O Nc6 8. a3
Bxc3 9. bxc3 dxc4 10. Bxc4 Qc7 11. Bd3 e5 12. Qc2 Re8 13. Nxe5 (13. e4 {
, for a long time considered White's most promising continuation, has been
dropped since the games Geller-Karaklajic and Averbakh-Ivkov from last year's
USSR-Yugoslavia match. The latter game went:} c4 14. Bxc4 exd4 15. cxd4 Na5 $1
16. Bb3 Qxc2 17. Bxc2 Nxe4 18. Re1 Bf5 {and a draw was agreed.}) 13... Nxe5 14.
dxe5 Qxe5 15. f3 b6 $6 (15... Bd7 16. Rb1 (16. Re1 $2 Ba4) 16... Bc6 17. c4
Rad8 $10 {Gligoric-Larsen, Moscow ol 1956}) 16. Re1 Bb7 17. e4 h5 18. Be3 (18.
f4 Qe7 19. e5 c4 $1 20. Bf1 (20. Bxc4 Qc5+ 21. Be3 Qxc4 22. exf6 Be4) (20. Bf5
Ng4 21. Bxg4 (21. Be3 Qh4 22. g3 Qh3 {/\ h4}) 21... Qh4 {/\ Qxg4}) 20... Ng4
21. h3 Qc5+ 22. Kh1 Nf2+ 23. Kh2 Nd3 24. Bxd3 cxd3 25. Qxd3 Rad8 $44) 18... h4
19. Bf1 (19. Rad1 $142 Bc6 {/\ Rad8/Nh5} (19... Rad8 20. Bb5)) 19... Rad8 {
(/\ Bxe4!?,Ng4~~)} 20. a4 (20. Qc1 $142) 20... Re6 21. Rad1 $2 (21. Qc1 $142)
21... Rxd1 (21... Red6 $6 22. Rxd6 Rxd6 23. Qc1 $14) 22. Rxd1 (22. Qxd1 $2 Qxc3
) 22... Bxe4 $1 23. Rd8+ Kh7 (23... Re8 $2 24. Rxe8+ Qxe8 25. fxe4) 24. Qf2 (
24. fxe4 Ng4 25. g3 Nxe3 26. Qf2 Nxf1 $19) 24... Bxf3 25. Qxh4+ Qh5 (25... Bh5
$6 26. Bg5 $40) 26. Bg5 $1 (26. Bd3+ Be4 27. Bxe4+ Rxe4 $17) (26. Qxh5+ Bxh5
27. Bf4 (27. Bg5 Ne4) 27... Be2 $17) (26. Qf4 Qg4 $17) 26... Qxh4 27. Bxh4 Bc6
(27... Be2 28. Bxe2 Rxe2 29. Bxf6 gxf6 30. Rd7 Rc2 31. Rxf7+ Kg6 32. Rxa7 Rxc3
33. Rb7 $10) 28. a5 $1 Ne4 29. axb6 axb6 30. Bc4 Rd6 (30... Rh6 $2 31. Be7 Nxc3
32. Bxf7 $16) 31. Bxf7 Rxd8 32. Bxd8 b5 33. Ba5 g6 34. Bb3 Kg7 35. Bc2 Kf6 36.
Bb6 Nxc3 37. Bxc5 Ne4 38. Bb4 Ke5 39. Kf1 Kd4 40. Ke2 Nc3+ 41. Kf2 Ne4+ {
Sources: BCM, March 1957, p78; CHESS, Vol.22, No.284-5, January 1957, p114} (
41... Ne4+ {The sealed move. A draw agreed without further play because of} 42.
Bxe4 Bxe4 {, with bishops of opposite colours.}) 1/2-1/2

