{I played rather rashly at the end when I should have lost.} 1. d4 Nf6 2. Nf3
b6 3. c4 e6 4. Nc3 Bb7 5. e3 Bb4 6. Bd2 c5 7. dxc5 bxc5 8. Be2 O-O 9. O-O d5
10. cxd5 exd5 11. Qb3 Qe7 12. Rfe1 Nc6 13. Rad1 (13. Nxd5 $2 Nxd5 14. Bxb4
Ndxb4 $19) 13... Rad8 14. Na4 Bxd2 15. Rxd2 Ne4 16. Rdd1 (16. Rdd1 Rfe8 17. Rc1
d4 18. Bb5 a6 19. Bxc6 $14) (16. Rxd5 Na5 17. Rxd8 Nxb3 18. Rxf8+ Kxf8 19. axb3
Ng5 20. Nd2 $15) 16... Rfe8 17. Nc3 {Now all is on d5} Nxc3 18. Qxc3 (18. bxc3
Ba8 (18... Na5 19. Qa3 $11)) 18... d4 {Black wins space} (18... Nb8 19. Qb3 Nc6
20. Bf1 Rb8 21. Qxd5 $15) (18... Nb4 19. a3 Nc6 20. Rc1 d4 21. exd4 cxd4 22.
Qc4 a5 $11) 19. exd4 Nxd4 {Menacing.} 20. Nxd4 cxd4 21. Qd2 Qd6 22. Bd3 Qd5 {
The mate threat is Qxg2} 23. Rxe8+ Rxe8 24. Bf1 Rd8 25. b3 h5 26. h3 Rd6 27.
Kh1 g5 28. f3 g4 $2 {Black gets more space} (28... Rd7 $5 $11) 29. Bc4 Qe5 30.
Re1 Qf6 31. fxg4 hxg4 (31... Qh4 32. gxh5 Qxh3+ 33. Kg1 $18) 32. Rf1 Qh4 33.
Rxf7 Bd5 34. Qf4 $2 ({Throws away a nice position.} 34. Rf4) 34... Qxh3+ {
Source: John Littlewood collection} (34... Qxh3+ 35. Qh2 Qxh2+ 36. Kxh2 Bxf7
$19) 0-1

